The present document is a player's primer to the Ashen learn-to-play adventure
you are about to play. While you are welcome to, you do not need to read the rulebook, and you do not need to make a character. This packet includes seven
pre-generated characters. You can use them as they come, change names or details,
or even, if none appeals, make your own. Discuss with the GM to make sure your
character fits with the parameters of the adventure.

This packet has three parts: this page, a short *How to Play*, and a *profile*
for each of the seven characters. Read this page, skim your profile, and let the
rules find you at the table.

== The World in Five Lines

The Last War ended and nobody won. The gods are dead, dying, or hiding. What
remains of the world is wrapped in *the Fog*: a roiling magical haze that rots
minds, warps machines, and makes travel a hazard rather than a chore.

People survive in *Clears*: pockets of thin Fog where crops grow and lungs
work. Between the Clears are ruins, wilderness, and the leftovers of a war
fought with magic and industry at the same time.

This is not to say that civilization is entirely nonexistent outside of the Clears:
the *Fogborn*, men adapted to the strange environment outside, and some of the
Deathless make their home there. But life is harder, people are fewer, and whosoever
would dwell in the Fog must be prepared to reckon with it.

== You Are Deathless

You died in the Last War. You did not stay dead.

You are one of the *Deathless*: an immortal veteran bound to the world until
whatever holds you here is finished. You remember only fragments: a face, perhaps,
or the feeling that someone, somewhere, owes you something --- and not much else. Ordinary people, insofar as anyone in this shattered world can be said to be normal,
find you useful, valuable, and a little frightening.

When you drop to 0 HP, you die. Then you get up again. You can spend *Essence*
to come back on the spot, or your soul returns to its anchor and you
reincorporate somewhere else, later.

#attention[
  For you, death is not the end, but die too much and you'll be out of the fight
  for a good couple of days at least. Plenty of time to make a getaway or beef up
  defenses.
]

== The Contract

The *Never-Still*, dreamers pledged to long-lost deities of the Faerie Realms, hold a share of *Venna Weald*, a large Clear in the northwestern forests of the one remaining continent. Old fey sites make the region valuable to them.

People around *Keshto Village*, a frontier settlement on the Weald's edge, have
been disappearing. First foragers and travellers. Then two of the Never-Still's own
peacekeepers. The disappearances are speeding up, and nobody local can explain
them.

So the Never-Still posted a *Black Guard contract* --- the closest thing the
Deathless have to a neutral, enforceable job offer --- for anyone willing to go
and find out why.

You took it.

== Why You Are Here

Each premade character's profile names a reason for their participation. If
you'd like to change it, or make your own character, here are the three broad
reasons why anyone would pledge their name at the Black Bazaar. 

- *Faction business.* You aren't here so much by choice as obligation. Someone above you wants this handled, or wants eyes on it.
- *The coin.* Black Guard contracts pay, and finishing one builds a name that
  gets you the next one.
- *Something personal.* There's something about these events that touches on business
  you have not finished with.

== Your Objective

Find out what is taking people. Find out where. Stop it.

Sounds simple --- but if it were trivial, the authorities of the Weald would
have dealt with it already. Be prepared to have to earn your pay, by hook, crook, 
or force. 
